# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

## Setup

```bash
conda env create -f environment.yml -p ./conda_env
conda activate ./conda_env
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pre-commit install && pre-commit install --hook-type commit-msg
```

If a committed `conda-lock.yml` exists, prefer
`conda-lock install --prefix ./conda_env conda-lock.yml`.

## Workflow

- Read the marked Repository contract in [`README.md`](README.md) before adding
  an artifact. It is the sole placement authority.
- Read root [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md), any nested agent instructions, and
  project-local additions before editing.
- Work on a topic branch and merge through a reviewed PR. Use Conventional
  Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`).
- Use test-driven changes for reusable library behavior. Do not weaken a gate or
  silently correct/drop data to make a run pass.
- Keep scientific choices, dataset bindings, topology, and executor resources
  in their distinct canonical configuration surfaces.

## Completion checklist

- [ ] Every created, moved, or generated file is in its canonical home with the
      required Git/DVC/ignore policy; accidental duplicates and temporary files
      are gone.
- [ ] `data/raw/` is byte-unchanged and no real/synthetic data crossed the
      raw/fixture boundary.
- [ ] Reusable computation has tests, types, and documentation; pipeline I/O is
      fully declared.
- [ ] Scientific pipeline changes include validated inputs/schema/unit of
      analysis, deterministic exemplars, per-unit and cohort QC, machine-readable
      metrics, provenance, and a reproducible command.
- [ ] `pytest -q` and `pre-commit run --all-files` pass, plus relevant Snakemake
      dry-run/end-to-end targets.
- [ ] No secret, cache, notebook output, generated result, or large payload is
      staged incorrectly.
- [ ] Documentation and migration notes reflect changed behavior or paths.
- [ ] Human-gated actions—factual metadata, raw/DVC mutation, run registration,
      interpretation, delivery freeze, research decision, or external record
      mutation—were either explicitly approved or clearly handed off as undone.

The rationale behind the contract is in
[`docs/structure.md`](docs/structure.md); it does not supersede the root matrix.
